<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Debug overlay. Replaces the pinned, https-only configuration in
    src/main/res/xml for debug builds only; a release APK contains that
    file and never this one.

    Two differences from it, and both are about the development server
    rather than about convenience:

    Cleartext is permitted, because the development server has no
    certificate. Pinning the certificate it does not have is not
    possible, and giving it a self-signed one would mean a trust anchor
    in the app for a key on somebody's laptop.

    There is no pin-set, for the same reason.

    What is NOT different: this is still the real network stack talking
    to the real service over the real wire. A debug build is how the
    airplane-mode test gets run, so it has to be the thing that is
    tested, not a mock.
-->
<network-security-config>

    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
